\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If $p_n$ is the $n$th prime, then the normalized prime gaps $(p_{n+1}-p_n)/\log p_n$ should be asymptotically distributed like an exponential random variable with density $e^{-x}$ for $0\leq x<\infty$.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2008/14}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
If $p_n$ is the $n$th prime, then the normalized prime gaps $(p_{n+1}-p_n)/\log p_n$ should be asymptotically distributed like an exponential random variable with density $e^{-x}$ for $0\leq x<\infty$.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30000934 (OWR-1795-001). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2008/14}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:30000934}

